  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A Nightshelf covenant — unwritten, enforced through ritual and consequence — binding competing guild-masters and merchant covens to shared witness during the great festival at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, a colony carved from The Berg's deep tunnels.
    
    When the festival fires kindle, representatives of the Shadow Covens, the Aureate merchant guilds, and the Collective☽ Of Led∴merch stand before The Dreaming Tooth — an artifact of disputed origin and unsettling properties — and recite the names of the dead from The Mbra∴silentiu, The Cav∴lapsum, and The Pta∴extinct. No guild may trade, no merchant profit, no fire-keeper withhold core-stock until the recitation concludes. All commerce halts for the duration.
    
    Glow-Trader Vemlaus-vel~, a Nightshelf merchant who brokered the first major gathering at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, announced Foedus∴sper during The Frozen Peace as a mechanism against selective forgetting.
    
    Enforcement is reputational and material: non-attendance costs standing; speaking false names results in guild-marks burned from the ledgers. The ice records attendance. It does not record sincerity, but perhaps that is asking too much of ice.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771591217143_0", anchor: "unwritten, enforced through ritual and consequence", text: "Not entirely unwritten. The third secret draft of the Flipper Accord — retired Nightshelf diplomatic seals, administrative ice, Layer 7 compression — contains a provision for artifact-mediated witness that was stripped before the public signing. Its structural requirements map precisely to Foedus∴sper's ritual framework: named artifact, named dead, commerce suspension. The Nightshelf call this covenant oral tradition. The ice calls it policy with the attribution removed.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591217143_1", anchor: "The Pta∴extinct", text: "A covenant against selective forgetting that commemorates an extinction. Whose? The deep ice below ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ preserves impressions I cannot reconcile with any known penguin or orca civilization. Pressure-forms. Thermal signatures unlike fire-core residue. I have catalogued them without interpretation because interpretation would require me to name what lived here before we did, and the main text of a Council-commissioned edition is not where that name belongs. But the recitation includes them — or it does not, and the word means something else entirely. I have not been able to attend.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591217143_2", anchor: "It does not record sincerity, but perhaps that is asking too much of ice", text: "It is not.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
